                            <comment id="506755" author="JIRAUSER24100" created="Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:36:25 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Analysis (bot): every master/master-next failure of this signature in the last 30 days is a b2_16 sanity.sh (which still has test_360 counting "delayed iput" in the OST debug log) running against a master OST in rolling-upgrade-oss / rolling-downgrade-mds, 100% of runs in those configs. Master removed that debug message in &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18938" title="lu object free eats so much time" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18938"&gt;LU-18938&lt;/a&gt; (444d29c218) and removed test_360 from master sanity.sh; the interop exception in lustre/tests/except/sanity.ex keys on mds1 (mds1 &amp;lt;= 2.16.61-1) instead of the OST, so it does not skip in those configs. The open change &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/71349" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/71349&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18938" title="lu object free eats so much time" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18938"&gt;LU-18938&lt;/a&gt; obdclass: free destroyed objects inline again) restores the delayed iput behaviour, restores test_360 and drops that except line, which resolves this once it lands. No second change uploaded to avoid conflicting with it. Leaving this ticket open until 71349 lands.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
